    <item>
      <title>eval : a security catastrope in waiting</title>
      <link>https://studiozenkai.com/post/eval-security-catastrophe/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Sep 2022 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://studiozenkai.com/post/eval-security-catastrophe/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;eval is one of Ruby&amp;rsquo;s most powerful methods. It’s also one of its most dangerous. When you use eval, you’re telling Ruby to treat a string as code and execute it. This opens the door to flexibility — but also to catastrophe.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
